      "observed": "The FCC VCAP pins are connected to pins on UART connectors rather than to local capacitors; the NAVC VCAP pins are unconnected.",
      "expected": "MCU VCAP pins should have the required local core-regulator capacitors and should not be routed to external interface connectors.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"23\") (name \"NET0030\") (node (ref \"FCC2\") (pin \"73\") (pinfunction \"VCAP\")) (node (ref \"UART3_FCC2\") (pin \"4\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"113\") (name \"NET0176\") (node (ref \"FCC2\") (pin \"48\") (pinfunction \"VCAP\")) (node (ref \"UART3_FCC2\") (pin \"3\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"274\") (name \"unconnected-(NAVC2-VCAP_1-Pad31)\") (node (ref \"NAVC2\") (pin \"31\") (pinfunction \"VCAP_1\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"275\") (name \"unconnected-(NAVC2-VCAP_2-Pad47)\") (node (ref \"NAVC2\") (pin \"47\") (pinfunction \"VCAP_2\"))"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "The MCU core regulator bypass requirements are not met, which can prevent correct MCU operation; routing FCC VCAP pins to connectors also exposes those pins to unintended external loading or connection.",
      "confidence": 0.98
    }
  ],
  "summary": "Anomalies are present: the MCU supply pins are disconnected from the regulator rail, the NAVC ground net is isolated from GND, and the MCU VCAP connections are missing or routed to connectors. These connectivity faults prevent the dual-MCU system from operating as intended."
}

